IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `au-interpretation-time`

-- Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (Australia): PART 5, General interpretation rules
-- (ss 12 to 25D). Only the provisions that decide something computable are encoded
-- here: s 13 (what is part of an Act), s 15AB(1) (extrinsic material), s 15B (coastal sea),
-- s 15C (jurisdiction), s 18B (titles), ss 25A to 25D. The interpretive canons (ss 12, 15A,
-- 15AA, 15AC, 15AD, 16 to 17A, 18A, 20, 21, 23) and the machinery-of-government
-- provisions (ss 19 to 19E) are `inert` in the coverage table, with a reason for each.
-- Sections 14, 14A, 14B, 15, 15AE, 17, 17AA, 18, 18C, 19BA to 19BD, 22, 22A, 22B, 22C, 24,
-- 25 and 25E are repealed (endnote 4).
-- LAYER 1: the law, objectively.

§ `Part 5: General interpretation rules`

§§ `Section 13: material that is part of an Act`

DECLARE `Material in the printed text of an Act` IS ONE OF
    `a section of the Act, or a Schedule to it, from the first section to the end of the last section or Schedule`
    `the long title`
    `a Preamble`
    `the enacting words`
    `a heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision appearing before the first section`
    `any other material`

-- src:312 | 13 Material that is part of an Act
-- src:313 | (1) All material from and including the first section of an Act to the end of:
-- src:314 | (a) if there are no Schedules to the Act—the last section of the Act; or
-- src:315 | (b) if there are one or more Schedules to the Act—the last Schedule to the Act;
-- src:316 | is part of the Act.
-- src:317 | (2) The following are also part of an Act:
-- src:318 | (a) the long title of the Act;
-- src:319 | (b) any Preamble to the Act;
-- src:320 | (c) the enacting words for the Act;
-- src:321 | (d) any heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision appearing before the first section of the Act.
-- src:322 | (3) However, text is not part of an Act, or a compilation of an Act within the meaning of the Legislation Act 2003, if the text:
-- src:323 | (a) only indicates the effect of an element of the Act; and
-- src:324 | (b) is accessible in an electronic version of the Act or compilation; and
-- src:325 | (c) does not appear in the printed text of the Act (or any amendment of the Act) as enacted by the Parliament, or any other printed version of the Act or compilation.
-- src:326 | Note: This text is known as alternative text or “alt text”. Alternative text may be accessible in an electronic version of an Act or compilation that is published on an approved website under the Legislation Act 2003. This text may, for example, aurally indicate the effect of a graphic image in an Act to assist users of the website who have visual disabilities.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 13(1) to (3) (src:312-326)
GIVEN material IS A `Material in the printed text of an Act`
      `it only indicates the effect of an element of the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is accessible in an electronic version of the Act or compilation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it does not appear in the printed text of the Act as enacted or in any other printed version` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is part of the Act` material `it only indicates the effect of an element of the Act` `it is accessible in an electronic version of the Act or compilation` `it does not appear in the printed text of the Act as enacted or in any other printed version` MEANS
        isListed
    AND (NOT (   `it only indicates the effect of an element of the Act`
             AND `it is accessible in an electronic version of the Act or compilation`
             AND `it does not appear in the printed text of the Act as enacted or in any other printed version`))
    WHERE
        isListed MEANS
            CONSIDER material
            WHEN `a section of the Act, or a Schedule to it, from the first section to the end of the last section or Schedule` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the long title` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a Preamble` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `the enacting words` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `a heading to a Chapter, Part, Division or Subdivision appearing before the first section` THEN TRUE
            WHEN `any other material` THEN FALSE

§§ `Section 15AB(1): extrinsic material`

-- The weighing in 15AB(3) (the desirability of relying on the ordinary meaning; avoiding
-- prolonging proceedings) is a judgment and is not encoded; it is `inert`.
-- src:331 | 15AB Use of extrinsic material in the interpretation of an Act
-- src:332 | (1) Subject to subsection (3), in the interpretation of a provision of an Act, if any material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision, consideration may be given to that material:
-- src:333 | (a) to confirm that the meaning of the provision is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act; or
-- src:334 | (b) to determine the meaning of the provision when:
-- src:335 | (i) the provision is ambiguous or obscure; or
-- src:336 | (ii) the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text of the provision taking into account its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable.
-- src:337 | (2) Without limiting the generality of subsection (1), the material that may be considered in accordance with that subsection in the interpretation of a provision of an Act includes:
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15AB(1) (src:331-337)
GIVEN `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`consideration may be given to the material` `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision` `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act` `the provision is ambiguous or obscure` `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable` MEANS
        `material not forming part of the Act is capable of assisting in the ascertainment of the meaning of the provision`
    AND (   `the use is to confirm that the meaning is the ordinary meaning conveyed by the text, taking account of its context in the Act and the purpose or object underlying the Act`
         OR `the provision is ambiguous or obscure`
         OR `that ordinary meaning leads to a result that is manifestly absurd or is unreasonable`)

§§ `Section 15B: the coastal sea`

-- src:366 | (4) In this section, coastal sea:
-- src:367 | (a) in relation to Australia, means:
-- src:368 | (i) the territorial sea of Australia; and
-- src:369 | (ii) the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea of Australia and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory;
-- src:370 | and includes the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea; and
-- src:371 | (b) in relation to an external Territory, means:
-- src:372 | (i) the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory; and
-- src:373 | (ii) the sea on the landward side of the territorial sea adjacent to the Territory and not within the limits of the Territory;
-- src:374 | and includes the airspace over, and the sea-bed and subsoil beneath, any such sea.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(4) (src:366-374)
GIVEN `it is in the territorial sea of Australia, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it is in the sea on the landward side of that territorial sea and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`is in the coastal sea of Australia` `it is in the territorial sea of Australia, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` `it is in the sea on the landward side of that territorial sea and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil` MEANS
    `it is in the territorial sea of Australia, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil`
    OR `it is in the sea on the landward side of that territorial sea and not within the limits of a State or internal Territory, or in its airspace, sea-bed or subsoil`

-- src:358 | 15B Application of Acts in coastal sea
-- src:359 | Coastal sea of Australia
-- src:360 | (1) An Act is taken to have effect in, and in relation to, the coastal sea of Australia as if that coastal sea were part of Australia.
-- src:361 | (2) A reference in an Act to Australia, or to the Commonwealth, is taken to include a reference to the coastal sea of Australia.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15B(1) and (2) (src:358-361)
GIVEN `it is in the coastal sea of Australia` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an Act is taken to have effect there as if it were part of Australia` `it is in the coastal sea of Australia` MEANS
    `it is in the coastal sea of Australia`

§§ `Section 15C: jurisdiction of courts`

DECLARE `Jurisdiction under section 15C` IS ONE OF
    `none vested by section 15C`
    `vested, and not limited by any limits to which the court's other jurisdiction is subject`
    `vested, so far only as the Constitution permits (a court of a Territory)`

-- src:375 | 15C Jurisdiction of courts
-- src:376 | Where a provision of an Act, whether expressly or by implication, authorises a civil or criminal proceeding to be instituted in a particular court in relation to a matter:
-- src:377 | (a) that provision shall be deemed to vest that court with jurisdiction in that matter;
-- src:378 | (b) the jurisdiction so vested is not limited by any limits to which any other jurisdiction of the court may be subject; and
-- src:379 | (c) in the case of a court of a Territory, that provision shall be construed as providing that the jurisdiction is vested so far only as the Constitution permits.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 15C (src:375-379)
GIVEN `a provision of an Act, expressly or by implication, authorises a civil or criminal proceeding to be instituted in a particular court in relation to a matter` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court is a court of a Territory` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Jurisdiction under section 15C`
`the jurisdiction the provision vests in the court` `a provision of an Act, expressly or by implication, authorises a civil or criminal proceeding to be instituted in a particular court in relation to a matter` `the court is a court of a Territory` MEANS
    IF   NOT `a provision of an Act, expressly or by implication, authorises a civil or criminal proceeding to be instituted in a particular court in relation to a matter`
    THEN `none vested by section 15C`
    ELSE IF   `the court is a court of a Territory`
         THEN `vested, so far only as the Constitution permits (a court of a Territory)`
         ELSE `vested, and not limited by any limits to which the court's other jurisdiction is subject`

§§ `Section 18B: titles of Chairs`

DECLARE `Chair title` IS ONE OF Chair, Chairperson, Chairman, Chairwoman

-- 18B(2) and (3): the office holder may choose a chair title or any other similar title;
-- if they have not, they may be referred to by the chair title that someone addressing
-- them considers appropriate. (The deputy chair titles of 18B(4) to (6) are the same rule.)
-- src:401 | 18B Titles of Chairs and Deputy Chairs
-- src:402 | Chair titles
-- src:403 | (1) For the purposes of this section, each of the following is a chair title:
-- src:404 | (a) Chair;
-- src:405 | (b) Chairperson;
-- src:406 | (c) Chairman;
-- src:407 | (d) Chairwoman.
-- src:408 | (2) A person occupying an office that is established by an Act and that has a chair title may choose to be referred to by:
-- src:409 | (a) that chair title; or
-- src:410 | (b) another chair title; or
-- src:411 | (c) any other similar title.
-- src:412 | (3) If a person occupying an office that is established by an Act and that has a chair title does not choose to be referred to by a title mentioned in subsection (2), the person may be referred to by the chair title that someone addressing the person considers appropriate.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 18B(1) to (3) (src:401-412)
GIVEN `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a chair title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has chosen to be referred to by this chair title, another chair title or a similar title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person has not chosen a title` IS A BOOLEAN
      `someone addressing the person considers this chair title appropriate` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the person may be referred to by this chair title` `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a chair title` `the person has chosen to be referred to by this chair title, another chair title or a similar title` `the person has not chosen a title` `someone addressing the person considers this chair title appropriate` MEANS
        `the person occupies an office established by an Act that has a chair title`
    AND (   `the person has chosen to be referred to by this chair title, another chair title or a similar title`
         OR (   `the person has not chosen a title`
             AND `someone addressing the person considers this chair title appropriate`))

§§ `Sections 25A to 25D`

-- 25A: a person who keeps a record of information by a mechanical, electronic or other
-- device, and is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document
-- containing it, or to make it available for inspection, is taken to be required to produce or
-- make available a writing that reproduces the information in a form capable of being
-- understood by the court, tribunal or person -- unless that court, tribunal or person
-- otherwise directs. Producing such a writing constitutes compliance.
-- src:591 | 25A Production of records kept in computers etc.
-- src:592 | Where a person who keeps a record of information by means of a mechanical, electronic or other device is required by or under an Act to produce the information or a document containing the information to, or make a document containing the information available for inspection by, a court, tribunal or person, then, unless the court, tribunal or person otherwise directs, the requirement shall be deemed to oblige the person to produce or make available for inspection, as the case may be, a writing that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the court, tribunal or person, and the production of such a writing to the court, tribunal or person constitutes compliance with the requirement.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 25A (src:591-592)
GIVEN `the person keeps the record by a mechanical, electronic or other device` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person is required by or under an Act to produce the information, or a document containing it, or to make it available for inspection` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the court, tribunal or person has otherwise directed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a writing that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the court, tribunal or person is produced or made available` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the requirement is complied with` `the person keeps the record by a mechanical, electronic or other device` `the person is required by or under an Act to produce the information, or a document containing it, or to make it available for inspection` `the court, tribunal or person has otherwise directed` `a writing that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the court, tribunal or person is produced or made available` MEANS
        `the person keeps the record by a mechanical, electronic or other device`
    AND `the person is required by or under an Act to produce the information, or a document containing it, or to make it available for inspection`
    AND (NOT `the court, tribunal or person has otherwise directed`)
    AND `a writing that reproduces the information in a form capable of being understood by the court, tribunal or person is produced or made available`

-- 25B(1) and (1A): when an Act (or a law of a State or Territory) alters the name of a body
-- or office, a reference to it under the former name is read as a reference to the new name,
-- except in relation to matters that occurred before the alteration took place.
-- src:594 | (1) Where an Act alters the name of a body (whether or not the body is incorporated) or alters the name of an office, then:
-- src:595 | (a) the body or office continues in existence under the new name so that its identity is not affected; and
-- src:596 | (b) in any Act, in any instrument under an Act, in any award or other industrial determination or order or any industrial agreement, in any other order (whether executive, judicial or otherwise), in any contract, in any pleading in, or process issued in connection with, any legal or other proceedings or in any other instrument, a reference to the body or the office under the former name shall, except in relation to matters that occurred before the alteration took place, be construed as a reference to the body or the office under the new name.
-- src:597 | (1A) Where a law of a State or Territory alters the name of a body (whether or not incorporated) or of an office, then a reference in an Act or an instrument made under an Act to the body or office under the former name is to be construed, except in relation to matters that occurred before the alteration, as a reference to the body or office under the new name.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 25B(1) and (1A) (src:594-597)
GIVEN `the reference relates to matters that occurred before the alteration took place` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`a reference to the former name is read as a reference to the new name` `the reference relates to matters that occurred before the alteration took place` MEANS
    NOT `the reference relates to matters that occurred before the alteration took place`

-- 25B(2): an Act altering the constitution of a body leaves its identity, functions, powers,
-- property, rights, liabilities, obligations and proceedings and inquiries unaffected.
-- src:598 | (2) Where an Act alters the constitution of a body (whether or not the body is incorporated), then:
-- src:599 | (a) the body continues in existence as newly constituted so that its identity is not affected;
-- src:600 | (b) the alteration does not affect any functions, powers, property, rights, liabilities or obligations of the body;
-- src:601 | (c) the alteration does not affect any legal or other proceedings instituted or to be instituted by or against the body, and any legal or other proceedings that might have been continued or commenced by or against the body as previously constituted may be continued or commenced by or against the body as newly constituted; and
-- src:602 | (d) the alteration does not affect any investigation or inquiry being or proposed to be undertaken by any tribunal, authority or person into any action taken or practice engaged in by the body before the alteration took place, and any investigation or inquiry that might have been continued or commenced into any such action or practice may be continued or commenced as if the action had been taken or the practice had been engaged in by the body as newly constituted.
-- src:603 | (3) In this section:
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 25B(2) (src:598-603)
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an alteration of the constitution of a body affects its identity, functions, powers, property, rights, liabilities or obligations, or pending proceedings, investigations or inquiries` MEANS FALSE

-- src:605 | 25C Compliance with forms
-- src:606 | Where an Act prescribes a form, then strict compliance with the form is not required and substantial compliance is sufficient.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 25C (src:605-606)
GIVEN `an Act prescribes a form` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the document substantially complies with the form` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the form requirement is met` `an Act prescribes a form` `the document substantially complies with the form` MEANS
    `an Act prescribes a form` AND `the document substantially complies with the form`

-- src:607 | 25D Content of statements of reasons for decisions
-- src:608 | Where an Act requires a tribunal, body or person making a decision to give written reasons for the decision, whether the expression “reasons”, “grounds” or any other expression is used, the instrument giving the reasons shall also set out the findings on material questions of fact and refer to the evidence or other material on which those findings were based.
@ref Acts Interpretation Act 1901 s 25D (src:607-608)
GIVEN `an Act requires a tribunal, body or person making a decision to give written reasons` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument giving the reasons sets out the findings on material questions of fact` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the instrument giving the reasons refers to the evidence or other material on which those findings were based` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`the written reasons are complete` `an Act requires a tribunal, body or person making a decision to give written reasons` `the instrument giving the reasons sets out the findings on material questions of fact` `the instrument giving the reasons refers to the evidence or other material on which those findings were based` MEANS
        `an Act requires a tribunal, body or person making a decision to give written reasons`
    AND `the instrument giving the reasons sets out the findings on material questions of fact`
    AND `the instrument giving the reasons refers to the evidence or other material on which those findings were based`
